window.ENCYCLOPEDIA_ENTRY_BODIES["note-notes-swirl-sequence-bundle-contracts"] = "Generated by `tools/build_swirl_sequence_bundle_contracts.py`. This joins the checked-in CE manifest, ebsrc `SWIRL_POINTER_TABLE`, local user-ROM-derived table bytes, and ignored EBDecomp swirl metadata into one payload-free contract.\n\nNo rendered swirl frames or ROM-derived payload bytes are checked in by this report.\n\n## Snapshot\n\n- CE `SWIRL_DATA` payload assets: `126`\n- CE `SWIRL_DATA` payload bytes: `29489`\n- pointer-table rows: `126`\n- primary-table rows: `7`\n- visible sequences: `6`\n- visible sequence frames: `126`\n- ignored EBDecomp PNG refs checked: `126`\n\n## Validation\n\n- `manifest_has_swirl_data_0_to_125`: `true`\n- `ebsrc_pointer_labels_match_payload_order`: `true`\n- `pointer_table_bytes_match_payload_starts`: `true`\n- `primary_rows_partition_visible_payloads`: `true`\n- `primary_rows_match_ebdecomp_frames_and_speed`: `true`\n- `ebdecomp_png_counts_match_primary_rows`: `true`\n\n## Primary Row Shape\n\n- bytes per row: `4`\n- inferred fields: `speed`, `first_payload_index`, `frame_count`, `reserved_zero`\n\n- Rows 1..6 match EBDecomp swirls.yml speed/frame counts.\n- The first/frame counts partition SWIRL_DATA_0..125 without overlap or gaps.\n- The pointer-table words match each SWIRL_DATA payload start address.\n\n## Sequence Rows\n\n| Sequence | Speed | First payload | Last payload | Frames | Primary bytes | Payload bytes | EBDecomp PNGs | Asset span |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 0 | 0 | - | 0 | `00 00 00 00` | 0 | 0 | null/disabled row |\n| 1 | 2 | 0 | 22 | 23 | `02 00 17 00` | 7341 | 23 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_0` `CE:6914..CE:691C` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_22` `CE:85B9..CE:85C1` |\n| 2 | 4 | 23 | 37 | 15 | `04 17 0F 00` | 2642 | 15 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_23` `CE:85C1..CE:85C9` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_37` `CE:8D94..CE:9013` |\n| 3 | 3 | 38 | 59 | 22 | `03 26 16 00` | 5538 | 22 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_38` `CE:9013..CE:9066` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_59` `CE:A5AD..CE:A5B5` |\n| 4 | 4 | 60 | 80 | 21 | `04 3C 15 00` | 9123 | 21 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_60` `CE:A5B5..CE:A5C6` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_80` `CE:C950..CE:C958` |\n| 5 | 2 | 81 | 108 | 28 | `02 51 1C 00` | 338 | 28 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_81` `CE:C958..CE:C960` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_108` `CE:CAA2..CE:CAAA` |\n| 6 | 3 | 109 | 125 | 17 | `03 6D 11 00` | 4507 | 17 | `asset.ce.swirl_data_109` `CE:CAAA..CE:CAB2` to `asset.ce.swirl_data_125` `CE:DC3A..CE:DC45` |\n\n## Runtime Contract\n\nThe portable contract is `swirl_sequence.N`: a sequence id selects one primary-table row, which gives playback speed, first CE `SWIRL_DATA` payload index, and frame count. Each frame index resolves through `SWIRL_POINTER_TABLE` to a raw `SWIRL_DATA_N` payload.\n\nThe primary table is now structurally understood well enough for ports and editors to preserve sequence identity and frame order. The internal `SWIRL_DATA` payload bytecode remains raw-preserved until a renderer needs to decode its drawing commands.\n\n## Runtime Evidence\n\n- `notes/c2-psi-swirl-overlay-tail-c2e6b3-c2ea74.md`: C2 overlay helpers start, poll, and close battle swirl overlay scripts while C4 callers select modes.\n- `notes/file-select-entity-scripts-and-swirl-transition-c4d830-c4d989.md`: C4 file-select/transition corridor corroborates overworld-facing swirl transition use.\n\n## Tables\n\n| Table | Range | Bytes |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n| `table.ce.214_data_battle_swirl_pointers_asm` (data/battle/swirl_pointers.asm) | `CE:DC45..CE:DD41` | 252 |\n| `table.ce.215_inline_swirl_primary_table` (inline:SWIRL_PRIMARY_TABLE) | `CE:DD41..CE:DD5D` | 28 |\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Promote sequence ids 1..6 to player-facing names only when caller-side mode names are corroborated.\n- Decode the internal SWIRL_DATA payload bytecode/shape if a future renderer or editor needs native geometry instead of preserved raw payloads.\n- Keep rendered EBDecomp PNG refs ignored; future local tooling can render previews from user-ROM-derived payloads.\n## Reference Context\n- Source: `notes/swirl-sequence-bundle-contracts.md`\n- Headings: Snapshot; Validation; Primary Row Shape; Sequence Rows; Runtime Contract; Runtime Evidence; Tables; Open Questions";
